art of a chow if I draw T5 or T8. T5 has 3 left, T8 has 3 left \u2013 decent chance. So maybe keep T6 and T7.  \n\nW2 is only one, could pair with another W2 (4 left in wall) or sequence with W1-W3, but W1 I have two, W3 has 4 left.  \n\nSo worst tiles are B8 and B1, also J1 maybe. But J1 is a dragon, could give \"Dragon Pung\" (2 points) if I make a pung, so maybe keep.  \n\nGiven scoring, Dragon Pung is only 2 points, not enough alone. But combined with other patterns could help reach 8.  \n\nI should consider what patterns are achievable:  \n- All Chows (2 points) \u2013 possible if I make all chows, but my exposed meld is a chow, and I could make more chows.  \n- Concealed Hand (2 points) \u2013 if I win by self-draw after all concealed melds except maybe the winning tile? But I already have an exposed meld, so \"Concealed Hand\" not possible.  \n- Self Drawn (1 point) possible.  \n- Edge Wait/Closed Wait/Single Wait possible later.  \n- Mixed Double Chow (1 point) if I have two chows in different suits same numbers.  \n- Pure Double Chow (1 point) if two identical chows in same suit.  \n- Short Straight (1 point) maybe.  \n- Two Terminal Chows (1 point) possible if I make chows of 123 and 789 in same suit.  \n- Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 point) \u2013 if I get a pung of W1 or J1 etc.  \n- One Voided Suit (1 point) \u2013 likely since I might discard all B or T.  \n- No Honors (1 point) \u2013 but I have J1, so if I discard J1, could aim for No Honors, but then lose Dragon Pung possibility.  \n- All Simples (2 points) \u2013 no terminals/honors, but I have terminals, so not possible unless I change hand drastically.  \n\nGiven the complexity, I should aim for a hand that can reach 8 points by combining several small patterns.  \n\nBut right now, I need to discard a tile. The safest discard is one that is unlikely to be used by others for Chow (since only previous player can Chow). Looking at game history:  \nPrevious player discarded B8, B9, W1, etc. My left opponent may not need B8 or B1.  \n\nI think B8 is the most useless tile in my hand: it's a middle tile (8) in a suit where 9 is exhausted, so no sequence with 9, and 7 is rare (only 1 left). B8 also not a terminal/honor, so no special value. B1 is a terminal, which could be useful for \"Pung of Terminals or Honors\" or \"Outside Hand\" but as said Outside Hand impossible.  \n\nDiscarding B8 keeps B1 which is terminal, maybe easier to use in a pung if I draw two more B1 (only 2 left in wall).  \n\nAlso, discarding B8 reduces the B suit, moving toward One Voided Suit (1 point) if I later discard all B tiles.  \n\nI'll choose to discard B8.  \n\nReason: B8 is isolated with poor sequence potential due to B9 exhausted and B7 scarce, and it doesn't contribute to potential scoring patterns as much as keeping terminals/honors or potential sequence tiles like T6/T7.  \n\nAnswer: Play B8"}
